This license lets eligible people and organizations use the Software with the freedoms of the MIT License or the
Apache License 2.0, at their choice, and keeps the Software away from businesses that kill animals. Everyone else
needs an Enterprise License from the Licensor. A plain-language summary is in LICENSE.vi.md (Vietnamese); it is not
part of this license, and this English text controls.

1. Definitions

"Software" means the work made available under this license, in source or object form, including modifications and
works derived from it.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license.

"Your Group" means You together with every entity that controls You, that You control, or that is under common
control with You. "Control" means direct or indirect ownership of more than 50% of the voting interests, or the power
to direct management and policies by contract or otherwise.

"Gross Revenue" means the total revenue of Your Group, consolidated, for its most recently completed fiscal year,
converted to United States dollars at the average exchange rate of that year. For an organization without revenue
(for example a non-profit or a public body) it means its total annual expenditure.

"Animal" means any non-human animal, including mammals, birds, fish, crustaceans, molluscs and insects.

"Prohibited Animal Product" means:
  (a) meat, poultry, fish, seafood, fur, leather, skins, gelatin, bone and any other product or ingredient obtained by
      killing an Animal;
  (b) fertilized eggs (eggs containing an embryo);
  (c) honey and other bee products, such as beeswax, royal jelly and propolis;
and any food, dish or product that contains one of them. Milk, unfertilized eggs and shorn wool are not Prohibited
Animal Products.

"Killing Activity" means any of:
  (a) slaughtering Animals, or processing Animals or their carcasses into Prohibited Animal Products;
  (b) commercial fishing, harvesting aquaculture for slaughter, hunting or trapping;
  (c) experiments or testing on Animals;
  (d) any other commercial activity of which killing Animals is a purpose.

"Food Service" means operating restaurants, cafes, bars, canteens, catering, delivery kitchens or any other business
that prepares or serves food or drink.

"Vegan Organization" means an organization all of whose products and services are free of Animal-derived ingredients
and materials and of testing on Animals.

2. Prohibited users

No rights are granted under this license, and You may not use the Software in any way, if any member of Your Group:
  (a) carries out any Killing Activity, at any scale;
  (b) carries out Food Service in which any Prohibited Animal Product is prepared, sold or served; or
  (c) derives more than 10% of its Gross Revenue from selling, distributing, processing, transporting, marketing or
      financing Prohibited Animal Products or Killing Activities, including retail and wholesale trade.

This section prevails over every other section of this license and applies equally to Enterprise Licenses (Section 5).

3. Free license for eligible users

If no member of Your Group falls under Section 2, and either
  (a) You are a Vegan Organization and every member of Your Group is a Vegan Organization, or
  (b) Your Group's Gross Revenue is less than USD 10,000,000,
then the Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
distribute and sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom You distribute it to do the same, under the
terms of either the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0, at Your choice, modified as follows:
  (i)   every copy of the Software You distribute, in source or object form, alone or as part of a larger work, must
        be licensed to its recipients under this license (SCaaS Community License 1.0), not under the MIT License or
        the Apache License 2.0 alone, and must include this license text;
  (ii)  the rights of each recipient depend on that recipient's own eligibility under Sections 2 and 3;
  (iii) Sections 2, 4, 5, 6 and 7 of this license apply in addition to, and take precedence over, the chosen terms.
If You choose the Apache License 2.0 terms, its patent license (Section 3 of that license), including its termination
on patent litigation, applies to You. Works You create that only call or link to the Software remain under the
licenses You choose for them; the Software within them stays under this license.

4. Growth beyond the threshold

If Your Group's Gross Revenue for a completed fiscal year reaches USD 10,000,000 or more, and You are not eligible
under Section 3(a), Your rights under Section 3 continue for 90 days after the end of that fiscal year, then end
unless You obtain an Enterprise License. If any member of Your Group falls under Section 2, Your rights end at once,
without a grace period.

5. Enterprise License

Anyone not eligible under Section 3 may use the Software only under a separate written Enterprise License from the
Licensor. To request one, contact the Licensor through https://github.com/dinhduongha/scaas. No Enterprise License is
granted to anyone who falls under Section 2, and every Enterprise License contains the conditions of Section 2: an
Enterprise licensee whose group later falls under Section 2 loses its rights as set out in Sections 4 and 6.

6. Eligibility, verification and termination

You are responsible for determining in good faith whether You are eligible. On the Licensor's written request You
will provide reasonable evidence of eligibility (for example financial statements or a description of Your Group's
business) within 30 days. Your rights under this license terminate automatically if You breach any of its terms or
become ineligible, and the Licensor may reinstate them only in writing. Termination does not affect recipients who
received the Software from You and remain eligible themselves.

